            <fr:title text="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality">(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>conjecture</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="thread">ns</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">open</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">scratch_nineteenth.md Result 13, items 15(e)--(f); result13_addendum.md; instruments ns_*.sage, mb_*.sage.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(NS). <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  N_{\mathrm {strict}} \le  N_z,
]]></fr:tex>
where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[N_{\mathrm {strict}}]]></fr:tex> is the nullity of the pairing on honest strict
Hom-triples and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[N_z]]></fr:tex> the centralizer-side count.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Role in the skeleton.</html:strong> This is the sole residue of the whole chain. By the exact ledger
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0046/" title="The Fredholm ledger" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0046/" display-uri="ffi-0046" type="local">the Fredholm ledger</fr:link>, multi-block <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link> follows
from it; and <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link> is the last open input to
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0035/" title="(P5): the grand formula off the unimodal locus" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0035/" display-uri="ffi-0035" type="local">(P5)</fr:link>, hence to <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link>. Everything else in the
growth program is proven.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Measured with equality, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[N_{\mathrm {strict}} = N_z]]></fr:tex>, 13/13 (mb_dual.sage).
Two independent reductions exist and neither has closed it:
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0047/" title="(Q-MOD): the reductive repair" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0047/" display-uri="ffi-0047" type="local">(Q-MOD)</fr:link> and <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0048/" title="The peeling induction" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0048/" display-uri="ffi-0048" type="local">the peeling induction</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Warning.</html:strong> ns_elim_defs.sage as committed is the pre-fix draft. Measure
(NS) only through ns_clean.sage or mb_dual.sage until it is
repaired.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0042/" title="Splits, flanks, tallness" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0042/" display-uri="ffi-0042" type="local">Splits, flanks, tallness</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0046/" title="The Fredholm ledger" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0046/" display-uri="ffi-0046" type="local">The Fredholm ledger</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0034/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0034</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0034/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions">(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">scratch_nineteenth.md Result (P4); certificates mlaw_close.py, o2_symbolic and o2_singular.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(P4). <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \max _{c \vdash  n} \operatorname {umod}(\mathfrak {n}_{c}) = \lfloor  n(n+6)/12 \rfloor ,
]]></fr:tex>
attained exactly by the period-6 maximizer shapes.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> Poset-interval induction (H10--H12): the argmax is shown
unimodal, so the maximum can be computed on the unimodal locus where
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link> is available in closed form, and the period-6 shapes
are exhibited as attaining it.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Consequence.</html:strong> With <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0037/" title="The growth theorem" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0037/" display-uri="ffi-0037" type="local">the growth theorem</fr:link> this makes the floor of
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0038/" title="The degree law" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0038/" display-uri="ffi-0038" type="local">the degree law</fr:link> unconditional at every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex>. It is also what
makes <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\lfloor  n(n+6)/12 \rfloor ]]></fr:tex> the right closed form to look for in the first
place.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0036/" title="(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0036/" display-uri="ffi-0036" type="local">(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0035/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0035</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0035/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="(P5): the grand formula off the unimodal locus">(P5): the grand formula off the unimodal locus</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">conditional</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">scratch_nineteenth.md Results H15--H17 and the 2026-08-21 finish-off (Theorem O); certificates p5_vtprime, p5_lemmaV_asym.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(P5). The grand formula of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link> extends to <html:em>all</html:em> compositions: <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \operatorname {umod}(c) = \text {grand}(\text {core}) + \sum _{\text {dips}}
  \binom {v+1}{2},
]]></fr:tex>
so that the non-unimodal case is the unimodal case plus an explicit dip
correction.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Reduced, not closed. The chain is H15--H17: H15 gives the
all-compositions formula (exact on 4083 rows, plus certified two-draw
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[z_u()]]></fr:tex> exhaustively at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 13]]></fr:tex> and at 14, 15); H16 gives the valley
cap <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[v \le  M_2(\text {core}) - 1]]></fr:tex> with packing and abstract
optimization, exact and violation-free for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[8 \le  n \le  40]]></fr:tex>, with the
tail closed by Theorem O; H17 is the section trick, reducing the
remaining content to <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link>. The sole residue is multi-block
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link>, hence <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Warning.</html:strong> The intermediate tool (P5<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[']]></fr:tex>) is <html:em>refuted</html:em> from <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 10]]></fr:tex> —
the deep valleys <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(4,1,5)]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(5,1,5)]]></fr:tex> overshoot. That is a failure
of the tool, not of (P5); do not cite p5_vt_check's "FAILURES" line,
which reports a superseded condition.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0036/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0036</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0036/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure">(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">scratch_nineteenth.md Result (P6), H7--H8.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(P6). For unimodal <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  e_0(c) = F(c') - F(c),
]]></fr:tex>
where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c']]></fr:tex> is the canonical unimodalization — the <html:em>collapse
identity</html:em>. So the defect term of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link> is itself in closed
form on the unimodal locus. Consequently <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F + e_0]]></fr:tex> is constant on
unimodalization classes and no argmax is spiky.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> H7, a copositive inequality whose extremal roots are those of
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x^2 - x + 1]]></fr:tex> — which is where the period <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[6]]></fr:tex> in <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> comes from, and
hence where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\lfloor  n(n+6)/12 \rfloor ]]></fr:tex> gets its <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[12]]></fr:tex>. H8 is the peak-shaving step:
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F + e_0 = F(c')]]></fr:tex> rules out spiky argmaxima, which is what
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0034/" title="(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0034/" display-uri="ffi-0034" type="local">(P4)</fr:link> needs to run its induction.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0032/" title="The graded count for z_u (H4)" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0032/" display-uri="ffi-0032" type="local">The graded count for z_u (H4)</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0040/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0040</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0040/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The M-law: the unimodal side of the leading-term law">The M-law: the unimodal side of the leading-term law</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">scratch_nineteenth.md H13--H13<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA['']]></fr:tex>; certificate mlaw_close.py.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>the M-law. The argmax count of the grand formula over unimodal
compositions satisfies <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  M_{\mathrm {unimodal}}(n) = n / \gcd (n, 6)
]]></fr:tex>
exactly, for all <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \ge  8]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> Three steps, H13--H13<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA['']]></fr:tex>. The sinusoidal move inequality
bounds the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[g]]></fr:tex>-oscillation by 1, with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\varepsilon  \in  \{0,1,2\}]]></fr:tex> and
mass <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(n\rho  - \kappa )/6]]></fr:tex>. Then a Diophantine classification of the
exact maximizers, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c \leftrightarrow  (\ell , t, a, \varepsilon )]]></fr:tex>: Lemma
A gives <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\rho  \in  \{r, r+6\}]]></fr:tex>, Lemma B gives <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\ell  \le  6]]></fr:tex>, Lemma C the
exact correspondence, with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\ell  = 4]]></fr:tex> isolated by <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[u_{\ell +1} = \pm  1]]></fr:tex>
and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\ell  = 5]]></fr:tex> giving families with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[u_6 = v_6 = 0]]></fr:tex>. Finally the case
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[6 \mid  n]]></fr:tex> closes by sinusoids.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Machine-verified <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  40]]></fr:tex> directly, and certified to
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  911]]></fr:tex> by mlaw_close.py over 40 stable types.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0034/" title="(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0034/" display-uri="ffi-0034" type="local">(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0036/" title="(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0036/" display-uri="ffi-0036" type="local">(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0032/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0032</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0032/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The graded count for z_u (H4)">The graded count for z_u (H4)</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">lc_law.md Corollary H4.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  z_u(c) = \sum _{k \ge  1} N_{k}(c) + e_0(c),
]]></fr:tex>
where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[N_{k}(c)]]></fr:tex> counts the pairs <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(s, t)]]></fr:tex> with
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[i(s) \le  i(t)+k \le  j(s) \le  j(t)+k]]></fr:tex>, and the defect term is <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  e_0(c) = \dim (\mathfrak {s} \cap  \operatorname {Ad}(\bar  g) \mathfrak {u}_L)
  \quad  \text {for generic } \bar  g \in  L.
]]></fr:tex></html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Consequence.</html:strong> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[z_u(c) \ge  \sum _{k \ge  1} N_{k}(c)]]></fr:tex> unconditionally,
i.e. <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[e_0(c) \ge  0]]></fr:tex>. This is the load-bearing exactness statement
under <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link>: the grand formula is the graded count plus a
defect that is proven non-negative, not estimated.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0031/" title="The thread algebra" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0031/" display-uri="ffi-0031" type="local">The thread algebra</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0037/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0037</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0037/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The growth theorem">The growth theorem</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">lc_law.md Theorem C, Corollary H6.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>For every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> and every prime power <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \kappa (U_{n}(\mathbb {F}_q)) \ge  q^{\lfloor  n(n+6)/12 \rfloor } \bigl (1 + O(q^{-1/2})\bigr )
]]></fr:tex>
along Frobenius towers in every characteristic. Consequently, where
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\kappa (U_{n})]]></fr:tex> is polynomial, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\deg  \kappa (U_{n}) \ge  \lfloor  n(n+6)/12 \rfloor ]]></fr:tex>; and combined
with <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0029/" title="Theorem D: the modality cap" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0029/" display-uri="ffi-0029" type="local">Theorem D</fr:link>, <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \operatorname {mod}(B : \mathfrak {n}_{n}) \ge  \lfloor  n(n+6)/12 \rfloor  - (n-1)
]]></fr:tex>
for every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex>, unconditionally.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> Rosenlicht plus Lang on the sweep strata. The generic strata
of maximal <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U]]></fr:tex>-modality each contribute
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q^{\operatorname {umod}}(1 + O(q^{-1/2}))]]></fr:tex> Frobenius-stable orbits, and
disjointness makes the contributions add. The floor is attained by the
explicit period-6 maximizer shapes of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0034/" title="(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0034/" display-uri="ffi-0034" type="local">(P4)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Warning.</html:strong> This re-proves Higman's <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q^{\lfloor  n(n+6)/12 \rfloor }]]></fr:tex> lower bound
(Vera-López--Arregi 2003 for small <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex>). Check
h2-literature-attribution before claiming new content here.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0026/" title="The class count kappa(U_n)" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0026/" display-uri="ffi-0026" type="local">The class count kappa(U_n)</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0029/" title="Theorem D: the modality cap" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0029/" display-uri="ffi-0029" type="local">Theorem D: the modality cap</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0034/" title="(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0034/" display-uri="ffi-0034" type="local">(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0031/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0031</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0031/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The thread algebra">The thread algebra</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">lc_law.md; journal sec:thread.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>Let <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\pi  : \mathfrak {p} \to  \mathfrak {l}]]></fr:tex> be the Levi projection, with kernel
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathfrak {n}_{c}]]></fr:tex>. The degree-0 part of the graded centralizer basis is
the <html:em>thread algebra</html:em> <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \mathfrak {s} = \pi (\mathfrak {z}(y_1)),
]]></fr:tex>
with basis elements <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  X_{s \to  t} = \sum _{a \in  I_s \cap  I_t} E^{(a)}_{t,s}
]]></fr:tex>
over index pairs with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[i(s) \le  i(t), j(s) \le  j(t), j(s) \ge  i(t)]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p>Here <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[I_s = [i(s), j(s)]]]></fr:tex> are the level intervals of the unimodal
level decomposition. This is defined for unimodal <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c]]></fr:tex> only:
non-unimodal <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c]]></fr:tex> has no density and no such decomposition, which is the
reason <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0035/" title="(P5): the grand formula off the unimodal locus" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0035/" display-uri="ffi-0035" type="local">(P5)</fr:link> is a separate and harder statement from
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0028/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0028</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0028/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="U-modality">U-modality</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">journal sec:modality.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>For a <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U]]></fr:tex>-stable irreducible subvariety <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[W \subseteq  \mathfrak {n}]]></fr:tex>,
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \operatorname {umod}(W) = \dim  W - \max _{y \in  W} \dim  U \cdot  y,
]]></fr:tex>
the dimension of the generic-orbit space; and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {umod}(w) =
\operatorname {umod}(\overline {\text {genStr}(w)})]]></fr:tex> per sweep stratum.</html:p>
            <html:p>For a composition <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c \vdash  n]]></fr:tex> with block sizes <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c_i]]></fr:tex>, write
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {umod}(\mathfrak {n}_{c})]]></fr:tex> for the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U]]></fr:tex>-modality of the parabolic
nilradical slice. These parabolic values are the ones with a closed
form: <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0001/" title="Setup: conjugation over a finite field" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0001/" display-uri="ffi-0001" type="local">Setup: conjugation over a finite field</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0027/" title="Borel modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0027/" display-uri="ffi-0027" type="local">Borel modality</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/sec-growth/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>sec-growth</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/sec-growth/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="finite-field-invariants: a reference forest › The growth program"><fr:link href="/ffi/index/" title="finite-field-invariants: a reference forest" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/index/" display-uri="index" type="local">finite-field-invariants: a reference forest</fr:link> › The growth program</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>Higman's class count, reached through the same Borel-orbit
  geometry. The chain from the definition of modality to the leading
  term of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\kappa (U_{n})]]></fr:tex> is complete except for one inequality, and the
  degree half of it is a theorem for every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:ul><html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0026/" title="The class count kappa(U_n)" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0026/" display-uri="ffi-0026" type="local">The class count</fr:link> — Higman's program.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0027/" title="Borel modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0027/" display-uri="ffi-0027" type="local">Borel modality</fr:link> — modality of the Borel on its
    nilradical.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0028/" title="U-modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0028/" display-uri="ffi-0028" type="local"><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U]]></fr:tex>-modality</fr:link> — modality of the unipotent
    group.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0029/" title="Theorem D: the modality cap" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0029/" display-uri="ffi-0029" type="local">Theorem D</fr:link> — the bridge to the class count.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local"><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[z_u(c)]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — the generic centralizer dimension.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0031/" title="The thread algebra" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0031/" display-uri="ffi-0031" type="local">The thread algebra</fr:link> — the algebra that computes it.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0032/" title="The graded count for z_u (H4)" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0032/" display-uri="ffi-0032" type="local">The graded count</fr:link> — the graded count and the defect.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link> — the closed form.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0034/" title="(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0034/" display-uri="ffi-0034" type="local">(P4)</fr:link> — the maximum, and where it is attained.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0035/" title="(P5): the grand formula off the unimodal locus" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0035/" display-uri="ffi-0035" type="local">(P5)</fr:link> — the off-unimodal extension.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0036/" title="(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0036/" display-uri="ffi-0036" type="local">(P6)</fr:link> — the collapse identity and the origin of
    period 6.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0037/" title="The growth theorem" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0037/" display-uri="ffi-0037" type="local">The growth theorem</fr:link> — the unconditional lower bound.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0038/" title="The degree law" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0038/" display-uri="ffi-0038" type="local">The degree law</fr:link> — the degree.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0039/" title="The leading-term law" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0039/" display-uri="ffi-0039" type="local">The leading-term law</fr:link> — the leading coefficient.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0040/" title="The M-law: the unimodal side of the leading-term law" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0040/" display-uri="ffi-0040" type="local">The M-law</fr:link> — its proven half.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0041/" title="(TOP-X): rigidity of maximal modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0041/" display-uri="ffi-0041" type="local">(TOP-X)</fr:link> — the rigidity statement it needs.</html:li></html:ul>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false" hidden-when-empty="true">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors />
        <fr:title text="Related">Related</fr:title>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0034/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0034</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0034/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions">(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">scratch_nineteenth.md Result (P4); certificates mlaw_close.py, o2_symbolic and o2_singular.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(P4). <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \max _{c \vdash  n} \operatorname {umod}(\mathfrak {n}_{c}) = \lfloor  n(n+6)/12 \rfloor ,
]]></fr:tex>
attained exactly by the period-6 maximizer shapes.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> Poset-interval induction (H10--H12): the argmax is shown
unimodal, so the maximum can be computed on the unimodal locus where
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link> is available in closed form, and the period-6 shapes
are exhibited as attaining it.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Consequence.</html:strong> With <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0037/" title="The growth theorem" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0037/" display-uri="ffi-0037" type="local">the growth theorem</fr:link> this makes the floor of
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0038/" title="The degree law" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0038/" display-uri="ffi-0038" type="local">the degree law</fr:link> unconditional at every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex>. It is also what
makes <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\lfloor  n(n+6)/12 \rfloor ]]></fr:tex> the right closed form to look for in the first
place.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0036/" title="(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0036/" display-uri="ffi-0036" type="local">(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0035/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0035</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0035/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="(P5): the grand formula off the unimodal locus">(P5): the grand formula off the unimodal locus</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">conditional</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">scratch_nineteenth.md Results H15--H17 and the 2026-08-21 finish-off (Theorem O); certificates p5_vtprime, p5_lemmaV_asym.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(P5). The grand formula of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link> extends to <html:em>all</html:em> compositions: <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \operatorname {umod}(c) = \text {grand}(\text {core}) + \sum _{\text {dips}}
  \binom {v+1}{2},
]]></fr:tex>
so that the non-unimodal case is the unimodal case plus an explicit dip
correction.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Reduced, not closed. The chain is H15--H17: H15 gives the
all-compositions formula (exact on 4083 rows, plus certified two-draw
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[z_u()]]></fr:tex> exhaustively at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 13]]></fr:tex> and at 14, 15); H16 gives the valley
cap <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[v \le  M_2(\text {core}) - 1]]></fr:tex> with packing and abstract
optimization, exact and violation-free for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[8 \le  n \le  40]]></fr:tex>, with the
tail closed by Theorem O; H17 is the section trick, reducing the
remaining content to <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link>. The sole residue is multi-block
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link>, hence <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Warning.</html:strong> The intermediate tool (P5<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[']]></fr:tex>) is <html:em>refuted</html:em> from <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 10]]></fr:tex> —
the deep valleys <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(4,1,5)]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(5,1,5)]]></fr:tex> overshoot. That is a failure
of the tool, not of (P5); do not cite p5_vt_check's "FAILURES" line,
which reports a superseded condition.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0036/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0036</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0036/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure">(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">scratch_nineteenth.md Result (P6), H7--H8.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(P6). For unimodal <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  e_0(c) = F(c') - F(c),
]]></fr:tex>
where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c']]></fr:tex> is the canonical unimodalization — the <html:em>collapse
identity</html:em>. So the defect term of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link> is itself in closed
form on the unimodal locus. Consequently <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F + e_0]]></fr:tex> is constant on
unimodalization classes and no argmax is spiky.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> H7, a copositive inequality whose extremal roots are those of
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x^2 - x + 1]]></fr:tex> — which is where the period <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[6]]></fr:tex> in <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> comes from, and
hence where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\lfloor  n(n+6)/12 \rfloor ]]></fr:tex> gets its <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[12]]></fr:tex>. H8 is the peak-shaving step:
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F + e_0 = F(c')]]></fr:tex> rules out spiky argmaxima, which is what
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0034/" title="(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0034/" display-uri="ffi-0034" type="local">(P4)</fr:link> needs to run its induction.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0032/" title="The graded count for z_u (H4)" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0032/" display-uri="ffi-0032" type="local">The graded count for z_u (H4)</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0032/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0032</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0032/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The graded count for z_u (H4)">The graded count for z_u (H4)</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">lc_law.md Corollary H4.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  z_u(c) = \sum _{k \ge  1} N_{k}(c) + e_0(c),
]]></fr:tex>
where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[N_{k}(c)]]></fr:tex> counts the pairs <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(s, t)]]></fr:tex> with
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[i(s) \le  i(t)+k \le  j(s) \le  j(t)+k]]></fr:tex>, and the defect term is <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  e_0(c) = \dim (\mathfrak {s} \cap  \operatorname {Ad}(\bar  g) \mathfrak {u}_L)
  \quad  \text {for generic } \bar  g \in  L.
]]></fr:tex></html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Consequence.</html:strong> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[z_u(c) \ge  \sum _{k \ge  1} N_{k}(c)]]></fr:tex> unconditionally,
i.e. <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[e_0(c) \ge  0]]></fr:tex>. This is the load-bearing exactness statement
under <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link>: the grand formula is the graded count plus a
defect that is proven non-negative, not estimated.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0031/" title="The thread algebra" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0031/" display-uri="ffi-0031" type="local">The thread algebra</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0030</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0030/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="z_u(c) and the modality formula">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">lc_law.md; journal sec:zu.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>Fix a composition <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c = (c_1, \dots , c_\ell )]]></fr:tex> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> and let
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y \in  \mathfrak {n}_{c}]]></fr:tex> be <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex>-generic. Write <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  z_u(c) = \dim (\mathfrak {z}(y) \cap  \mathfrak {u}),
]]></fr:tex>
the dimension of the centralizer of a generic element inside the upper
triangular nilpotent Lie algebra.</html:p>
            <html:p>For parabolic slices the modality is then <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \operatorname {umod}(\mathfrak {n}_{c}) = d_c - \frac {n(n - 1)}{2} + z_u(c),
  \qquad  d_c = \sum _i c_i^2 - n,
]]></fr:tex>
where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[d_c]]></fr:tex> adjusts the flag count. So computing <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {umod}(\mathfrak {n}_{c})]]></fr:tex>
is computing <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[z_u(c)]]></fr:tex>, which is what <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0032/" title="The graded count for z_u (H4)" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0032/" display-uri="ffi-0032" type="local">the graded count</fr:link>
does.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0028/" title="U-modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0028/" display-uri="ffi-0028" type="local">U-modality</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
